\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Up Midmorning; Highest Against Dlr In 11 Mos \b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Oktober 1998\par 05:24\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht (THB) is higher against the dollar in Asian spot trading midmorning Friday, in line with most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after a sudden cut in U.S. interest rates, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said there was no evidence so far of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after the dollar fell below THB38.00 late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  At 0300 GMT (11.00 p.m. Thursday EDT), the dollar is at THB37.85, down from THB37.905 at the close of trading Thursday. The baht is now at its highest level against the dollar in 11 months, or since Nov. 10 last year. \par \par \uc2  The Federal Reserve cut U.S. interest rates a further 25 basis points overnight, after cutting rates by the same amount late last month. It cited concerns over a potential credit crunch for its decision to cut rates in the period between its regular policy-setting board meetings. \par \par \uc2  The federal funds rate now stands at 5.00%, from 5.25%, and the discount rate was lowered to 4.75%, from 5.00%. \par \par \uc2  The action drove the dollar down to Y115.45, before it bounced back to present levels around Y116.55. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said investors sold dollars after the Fed cut, boosting most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region. \par \par \uc2  "The baht could have been at 37 to dollar since last week if there were no \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  then," said a dealer at Banque Nationale de Paris. Local dealers said the Bank of Thailand bought dollars last week to slow down the rise of the baht. Bank of Thailand officials did not deny it, but said they bought dollars for the settlement of forward foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  contracts. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 16-10-98 \par \par \uc2  0324GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010917duag005xr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
