\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Thailand \highlight\uc2  to keep baht  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  to minimum. \b0\par\par\uc2 221 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 1998\par 06:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, June 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep to the minimum any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the baht, Deputy Prime Minister Supachai Panichpakdi said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  But he told reporters that Thailand was still concerned about the fate of Chinese yuan and would brace itself to handle problems that might result from any steep depreciation of the Chinese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as little as possible and allow the baht to be dictated by the international economy," Supachai said. \par \par \uc2  "We might adjust interest rates from time to time but we will no longer rely too much on raising interest rates too high to keep the baht stable," he said. \par \par \uc2  Separately, Finance Minister Tarrin Nimmanahaeminda welcomed the move by the Federal Reserve and Bank of Japan to jointly support the yen through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He said the move would curb speculative attacks on the yen near-term but stressed that a longer term solution would require fiscal policy adjustments and sorting out of problems among financial institutions. \par \par \uc2  Tarrin said the baht, which rose on the back of the stronger yen, helped release some pressure on short-term interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one-day bond repurchase was quoted at 17.75 percent this morning versus 19.00 percent late on Wednesday, he said. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du