\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht, stocks seen extending losses this week. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Phisanu Promchanya \par \uc2 441 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 1998\par 03:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, June 7 (Reuters) - The Thai baht, which last week plunged through the 40 per dollar level after holding out in the 38-40 range since mid-March, is widely expected to ease toward 45 but will be influenced by the yen's movement, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai stock market would likely see some technical rebounds early this week before giving way to profit-taking as market sentiment remains cloudy, with no positive signs in sight, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai SET index ended at 318.16 on Friday against 325.59 a week earlier. \par \par \uc2  "The market might see a small technical rebound early this week but should later head steeply down, probably below 300," said Somchai Prasertsilpa, senior analyst at Thai Sakura Finance and Securities. \par \par \uc2  Russel Kopp, head of research at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson, agreed: "At some point in the next few weeks, the index could easily go under 300." \par \par \uc2  Investors are nervous about volatile regional money and equity markets, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The jitters over a second Asian financial crisis and weak regional stocks keep investors on edge," said Somchai. \par \par \uc2  Kopp said the market remained concerned over the health of local financial institutions and their recapitalisation problems. \par \par \uc2  Financial institutions raising capital include the Siam Commercial Bank Plc, the fourth largest bank, which announced a massive capital increase plan in late May. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's defence of the baht through its market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rocked Thai stocks as its short-term interest rate hikes were not expected to be sufficient and the bank may be forced to use more foreign reserves to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The baht's defence may require more than the interest rate mechanism. It would further erode foreign reserves, something investors do not want to see," said Somchai. \par \par \uc2  The baht is expected to retreat closer to 45 per dollar, its expected strong support seen being defended by the government, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "I believe the baht will trade in the 41.50-45.00 range this week," said Satian Tantanasarit, senior vice president at Thai Danu Bank Plc. \par \par \uc2  "If the yen continues to fall, it would add pressure on the baht," said one senior dealer at a large Thai bank. \par \par \uc2  The baht's limited market supply would restrain foreign speculation against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulation prohibiting forward offshore contracts of over 50 million baht remains effective and it will limit baht supply available for speculators," Satian said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Friday he was satisfied with the baht's range of 42-43 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6703ldx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
