\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends At 12-Week Low In Asian Spot Trading \b0\par\par\uc2 291 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 1998\par 13:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (Dow Jones)--The Thai baht (THB) slumped in Asian spot trading Friday, crossing the THB43 to the dollar level for the first time in 12 weeks amid growing fears that the Asian economic crisis is deepening. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also sank in the swap market, where investors make agreements to buy and sell baht at fixed prices at fixed times in the future. Swap premiums rose amid vigorous dollar-buying, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At the close of Asian spot trading Friday, the dollar was at THB43.25, its highest level since March 12 and up from THB42.45 at the close of trading Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers attributed the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slump to worries that the recovery of crisis-stricken Asian economies is stalling as the Japanese economy deteriorates. \par \par \uc2  Thailand, for example, expects to see its economy shrink 5.5% in 1998, a bigger contraction than the government initially predicted. Japan is Thailand's biggest trading partner and its biggest bank lender. \par \par \uc2  "Worries are flaring up again about the health of the region's economies," said a dealer at a U.S. bank. \par \par \uc2  To halt the decline of the baht, the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday raised repurchase rates for the second time in a week and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in offshore spot markets. But the effect of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was fleeting, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , set its reference rate at THB42.806 to the dollar Friday, up from THB41.719 Thursday. The reference rate is a weighted average of rates charged by Thai commercial banks the previous trading day. It serves as a benchmark for domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 05-06-98 \par \par \uc2  1110GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6504u9v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
