\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -2: Baht Crashes To 3-Month Low Vs US$ \b0\par\par\uc2 303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 1998\par 12:16\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the Bank of\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  failed, and that adversely affected market\par psychology," said Chua Soon Hock, chief strategist at Sanwa\par Bank in Singapore.\par    The effect of the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's action - in which\par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the swap market to push up\par offshore interest rates in addition to selling U.S. dollars\par in the spot market - proved short-lived as market\par participants once again began buying U.S. dollars on Friday\par morning.\par    "Once we hit THB42.00, the Thai corporates panicked and\par started buying up dollars to cover their requirements. The\par Bank of Thailand was in the market earlier but they appear to\par have given up now, so the dollar is up again," said a baht\par trader at a U.S. bank in Singapore.\par    In late Asian trading the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was quoted at\par THB43.12, up from THB42.6750 late on Thursday and at its\par highest level in nearly three months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Over the coming week a test higher up to THB45.00 is\par inevitable, he said, "Unless the Bank of Thailand pushes\par short-term rates up to silly levels, around 100% to 200%."\par Even then, given the underlying level of dollar demand, the\par U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is likely to find support around THB42.50, said\par the trader.\par    "Sporadic \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by individual central banks is not\par effective. What is required is well conceived co-ordinated\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Asian central banks acting in unison," said\par Chua.\par    The commitment of just a small fraction of Asian central\par banks combined reserves of over $700 billion would be\par sufficient to cause a sea change in market sentiment and\par reverse the downward trend of Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , argued Chua.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  06-05-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0616EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du6501dbv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
