\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mostly Dn Early; Baht Up On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 389 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 1998\par 03:44\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--Southeast Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are\par mostly lower in early trading on Friday morning, although the\par Thai baht has rallied from Thursday's lows on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by\par the Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in both the spot and swap markets.\par    "The dollar buying interest is still very strong,\par although with the high interest rates we are seeing on the\par ringgit and the baht the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may stabilize," said the\par head of trading at a Japanese bank in Singapore.\par    Late Thursday the Bank of Thailand sold U.S. dollars in\par the spot market, pushing the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  below the 43.00\par baht (THB) level breached earlier. Traders said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also active in the swap market, pushing up offshore\par interest rates, making the the baht more expensive to sell\par short.\par    "If the swap rates go up any further I think we will see\par the spot rate back below THB42.00," said the Japanese bank\par trading chief.\par    At 0130 GMT (9:30 p.m. Thursday EDT) the U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  dollar was\par quoted at THB42.6000, down from THB42.6750 late the previous\par day. The implied yield on the one month U.S. dollar/baht swap\par was at 53.60%, up from 35.10% late on Thursday.\par    Against other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the U.S. dollar\par remains well bid, despite steps towards resolving the debt\par problems of Malaysia and Indonesia.\par    "This is all being discounted. The market is so used to\par bad news about Asia, it is unable to believe good news," said\par a regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trader at a U.K. bank in Singapore.\par    Against the ringgit, the U.S. dollar is quoted at 3.7960\par ringgit (MYR), up from MYR3.9700 late the day before.\par    In Singapore, the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is at S$1.6891, up from\par S$1.6834.\par    Against the rupiah the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is at 11,550 rupiah\par (IDR), unchanged from the previous day, although bid/offer\par spreads have narrowed.\par    Traders say despite the U.S. dollar's current bid tone,\par the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is likely to weaken against the regional\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  later in day, as players close out long U.S.\par dollar positions ahead of the weekend.\par    -By Tom Holland; 65 421 4800\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires  06-04-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2144EDT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du6501d3q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
