\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht weaker late on offshore dollar demand. \b0\par\par\uc2 271 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 1998\par 12:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, June 5 (Reuters) - The Thai baht was weaker in late trade on Friday as offshore demand for dollars continued to buffet the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Losses were capped by fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, they added. \par \par \uc2  The baht was quoted at 43.05/43.20 per dollar in late trade on Friday against 42.85/42.95 per dollar in early morning. \par \par \uc2  "When the dollar is moving, a lot people are looking for reasons related to fundamentals...I think people are just looking for a (dollar) stampede by foreigners," said a dealer from a local bank. \par \par \uc2  The weakening yen may have unnerved the market but there was little evidence to suggest that the baht was tracking it, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The market appeared to believe the foreign demand would push the baht to test 45 per dollar next week despite continued dollar selling from Thai exporters, they added. \par \par \uc2  Foreigners were also increasingly active in the forward market, they added. \par \par \uc2  Offshore one month forward swap rates were up at 145/175 satangs per dollar in the evening against 115/125 in the morning. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's one day bond repurchase rate closed at 19 percent but fears of Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rather than high short term interest rates helped cap the baht's slide, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Large local banks quoted overnight interbank rates at 19.00-20.00 percent against 19.50-20.00 percent in the morning, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  - Bangkok Newsroom (662) 253-5000 ext 414 \par \p