\par\par \b \uc2  SE Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  -2: Regional Rally Remains Fragile \b0\par\par\uc2 283 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Februar 1998\par 12:42\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The fragility of the rally was emphasized by one\par prominent regional economist, who privately estimates that\par current negotiations on restructuring Indonesia's estimated\par $65 billion of private sector short-term debt have no more\par than a 60% chance of success.\par    Progress will be hampered, he said, by the opacity of\par the Indonesian financial system, the inefficiency of\par Indonesian bureaucracy and by the country's continuing\par political uncertainty.\par    After rising against the U.S. dollar last week, the\par rupiah dropped back on Monday. In late Asian trading, the\par U.S. dollar was quoted at IDR10,495, up from IDR10,300 at\par midday on Friday and IDR10,250 late Tuesday as trading wound\par down ahead of the holiday. Many traders said the U.S. dollar\par would have broken up through the IDR11,000 mark on Monday,\par save for the threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The baht, meanwhile, finished higher following the\par dismantling of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's two-tier \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par as baht purchases from offshore market participants\par outweighed domestic demand for U.S. dollars. In late trading\par the U.S. dollar was quoted at THB51.54, down from THB54.00\par in the offshore market midday Friday and THB53.25 late\par Wednesday.\par    Boosted by the baht, the ringgit also rose. In late\par Asian trading, the U.S. dollar was at MYR4.1950, lower from\par MYR4.3775 on Friday and MYR4.4050 late Tuesday.\par    Against the Singapore dollar the U.S. dollar dropped to\par S$1.7194, from S$1.7300 on Friday and S$1.7345 on Tuesday.\par    Volumes remained scant, however, as many participants\par hung back from the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires  02-02-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0642EST\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010916du2200aa9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
