\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Thailand \highlight\uc2 /Ctrl Bank/ \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -3: Probe By Crime-Buster \b0\par\par\uc2 294 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 1997\par 14:11\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Duangmanee, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokeswoman, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was increasing its inspections of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions at commercial banks. \par \par \uc2  She declined to say how many transactions had been scrutinized or whether any violations had been found. \par \par \uc2  Thai and foreign bankers said they had seen no additional scrutiny. \par \par \uc2  'There's information submitted every day by commercial banks to the Bank of Thailand,' said James Roe, a treasury manager at Chase Manhattan Bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  'It's normal practice to give information at the end of the day, and for the Bank of Thailand to ask about certain transactions. There hasn't been an unusual number of inquiries from the bank recently.' \par \par \uc2  Thai officials have frequently attributed trouble in the country's financial markets to foreign mischief, usually by \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  or stock market speculators. \par \par \uc2  In July, Thai police raided the offices of two securities houses, ABM-AMRO Hoare Govett Asia Investment Research Ltd. and Capital Nomura PCL, amid rumors five Thai banks were about to fail. The raids resulted in no prosecutions. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the Bangkok Post newspaper said the country's top crime-buster, Police Lt.-Gen. Seri Temiyavej, was investigating companies suspected of having caused the baht's steep fall this week. Seri couldn't be reached for comment. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers said the baht's slump this week was the result simply of a rush by Thai corporations to repay an estimated $6 billion foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt due in December. \par \par \uc2  'What's driving the exchange rate is a general need by customers to hedge their exposure,' Roe of Chase Manhattan said. 'That typically comes to a crescendo at the end of the year.' \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-12-97 \par \par \uc2  1311GMT \par \par \uc2  1144 4279 55129 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtch09pmn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
