\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Thailand \highlight\uc2 /Ctrl Bank/ \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  -2:Peregrine's Dlr Purchases \b0\par\par\uc2 324 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Dezember 1997\par 13:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, a Thai newspaper reported that Peregrine Finance & Securities, a unit of Hong Kong's Peregrine Investments Holdings Ltd., had been asked to explain unusually-large recent purchases of dollars. \par \par \uc2  Duangmanee declined to say whether Peregrine was formally under investigation, and a top Peregrine executive declined to comment. \par \par \uc2  'All I can say is the transactions were carried out in the normal course of business,' said Christopher Jackson, Peregrine's executive chairman in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made commitments to spend as much as $23 billion baht in forward \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets this year before finally abandoning its defense of the country's fixed exchange-rate system. \par \par \uc2  The baht has since fallen 45% against the dollar, putting many debt-ridden Thai corporations on the brink of insolvency. \par \par \uc2  The forward commitments have been a steady drain on the country's foreign reserves, which have been stabilized only by regular cash infusions by the IMF. \par \par \uc2  In the last two weeks of November, the Bank of Thailand repaid $2.1 billion of its forward commitments, bringing reserves down to a three-month low of $26.3 billion. \par \par \uc2  Under an agreement with the IMF, which provided a $17.2 billion bailout for Thailand, the country must maintain reserves of at least $23 billion this year. \par \par \uc2  That has restricted the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ability to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, bankers said. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  still retains other means of control, including anti-speculation regulations and tough talk, or 'moral suasion,' bankers said. \par \par \uc2  In May, to fight \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators, the Bank of Thailand ordered Thai commercial banks to stop selling baht to foreigners unless they could prove the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't be used for speculation. \par \par \uc2  The controls created a two-tier \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in which foreigners pay a steeper rate to buy baht than local investors do. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 17-12-97 \par \par \uc2  1247GMT \par \par \uc2  1144 4279 55129 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dtch09pig\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
