\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS-Thai baht dives, little sign of BOT support. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Vithoon Amorn \par \uc2 550 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Dezember 1997\par 09:04\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Dec 12 (Reuters) - Thai leaders said on Friday the battered baht was hard pressed to resist sustained regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil but dealers said they did not detect any clear signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The baht hit its all-time low of 45.30 to the dollar at around 0500 GMT, after it opened at 44.30/44.60 and against 43.50/43.60 late on Thursday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Chaiyawat Wibulswadsi said: "At a time like this, we are hard pressed to resist the trend but we will try to slow down any rapid slide of the baht. We should not be panicked by news reports." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealers were divided on whether or not  the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOT) had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the baht. \par \par \uc2  A senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at Bank of Asia Plc, said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have stepped in when the baht fell to nearly 45.00 to the dollar in late morning. But any such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was small as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  resumed its slide shortly after, she said. \par \par \uc2  The baht stabilised at 44.65/44.95 by 0749 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "Some dollar bids were quickly liquidated. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  but the amount must have been small, likely not more than $20 million. The authorities have indicated they have no intention to use too much money to do this," she said. \par \par \uc2  Prime Minister Chuan Leekpai on Friday appealed for public calm and said his government was determined to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through consistent economic measures. \par \par \uc2  Chuan said he and Finance Minister Tarrin Nimmanahaeminda closely monitored regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets but his government would not take any action that could aggravate the baht's weakness. \par \par \uc2  Chuan blamed the baht's new low on heavy fresh setbacks of the South Korean won and the Indonesian rupiah on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The heavy impact from South Korea and Indonesia is being felt widely throughout the region. We must accept the fact that this is unavoidable," the prime minister said. \par \par \uc2  A dealer at a foreign bank said some U.S. bank branches were active dollar bidders, partly induced by sustained tumbling of the won and rupiah. \par \par \uc2  Another trader at Bank of Ayudhya Plc, said the baht would look quite defenceless if the rupiah retreated below 5,000 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Later the rupiah did pierce that level and at 0742 GMT was quoted at 5,015/5,065 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  A trader at Bank of America said year-end commercial dollar demand was evident on Friday in Thailand with foreign oil firms among major bidders. \par \par \uc2  He expected the baht to consolidate at about 45.00 if the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis did not intensify next week. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Tarrin said on Friday Thailand needed to keep short-term domestic interest rates high to help slow a sustained slide of the baht. \par \par \uc2  Tarrin told reporters he regarded the baht's early stability as more vital and urgent than easing heavy financing burdens faced by Thai businesses. \par \par \uc2  "On interest rates, we will keep them temporarily high to help ease domestic problems. Stability of our exchange rate is more important," he said. \par \par \uc2  -- Bangkok newsroom (662)-652-0642 \par \par \uc2  -- e-mail: bangkok.newsroom@reuters.com \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011003dtcc01797\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
