\par\par \b \uc2  Asian cooperation on  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  a way off-analysts. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Phil Smith \par \uc2 646 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Sept 17 - This week's meeting of seven ASEAN finance ministers in Bangkok will not specifically address cooperation on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which analysts said on Wednesday would be years in the making. \par \par \uc2  "There is no topic, it will be an informal meeting," said Somkid Jatusipitak, adviser to Thai Finance Minister Thanong Bidaya. \par \par \uc2  Ministers from seven Association of South East Asian Nations (ASEAN) will hold talks on Thursday, one day ahead of the Asia Europe Meeting (ASEM) of finance ministers. \par \par \uc2  When asked about local newspaper reports that the ministers had decided to delay talks on how to deal with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis, he said: "No, I said they would discuss cooperation in general. We don't want to have any set position ahead of the ASEM meeting." \par \par \uc2  His reaction came as no surprise to analysts who said the region's macro-economic house had first to be put in order before any solid plans could be laid down to cooperate on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  And that, they said, could take years. \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  cooperation requires coordination of economic policy formulation," said P.K. Basu, regional economist at UBS Securities in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "If a country's economic policies don't gain the confidence of its neighbours then those neighbours will be somewhat less willing to cooperate to defend it's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  cooperation is easier said than done." \par \par \uc2  While reserves around the Asian region are substantial, analysts said it is not a simple matter of countries banding together with coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  come under pressure. \par \par \uc2  As May's Thai baht debacle showed, such a cooperation could turn out to be a bottomless pit and analysts doubt cash-rich countries would be willing to take the risk. \par \par \uc2  "It's fine to talk about cooperation in markets but I can't see the richer nations signing up to such a deal when there are major economic problems still to be solved," said one Singapore-based analyst who preferred not to be named. \par \par \uc2  "I mean Thailand has already spent billions defending the baht and to no avail, I can't see other countries signing up to any agreement on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the economic situation settles down." \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Thanong Bidaya has said baht \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will deplete \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's reserves by six to 14 billion dollars over the next year. The International Monetary Fund is spearheading a $17.2 billion international bailout package aimed at rebuilding Thailand's reserves situation. \par \par \uc2  There is also the background problem of the baht devaluation itself. Analysts said it was far from clear whether Thailand's neighbours were warned about the devaluation and that could well have raised a few hackles. \par \par \uc2  "The devaluation had a big impact on the rest of Southeast Asia and on that there was much less evidence of coordination and cooperation than there was in May during the initial attack on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," UBS's Basu said. \par \par \uc2  There is already a repo agreement in place which is designed to help countries with \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  problems, but this is designed to help with liquidity rather than providing asset power to try to stop any decline in a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The system works by allowing a country to place its holding of U.S. Treasury bonds with another \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  for dollars on the spot market. The system simply allows a country to get hold of U.S. dollars quickly, and at attractive rates, using their U.S. Treasury paper as collateral. \par \par \uc2  "For any rock-solid agreement on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  cooperation you need to have similar monetary conditions in each country," said Chiang Yao Chye, Head of Asia Pacific Research at CIBC in Singapore. "Otherwise who is to determine at what rate a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be and why should one country spend its reserves to prop up another when it could be overvalued?" \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011001dt9h02d9a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
