\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Thailand \highlight\uc2 /Baht Ends -2: Despite  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 1997\par 13:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht slumped to a new record low in domestic spot trading Wednesday, hurt by brisk dollar-buying by Thai corporations nervous about the continued depreciation of the baht, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move to prop up the baht later in the session Wednesday - by aggressive dollar-selling - failed to take the heat off the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. Investors, in fact, rushed to buy dollars from the Bank of Thailand to take advantage of the attractive exchange rate, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  At the close of trading Wednesday, the dollar was at 37.85 baht in the domestic spot market - the level dealers said was the highest in history. At that rate, the dollar was 7.7% above its closing level of 35.15 baht Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  also closed at a historic high in the offshore market, at 35.55 baht Wednesday from 34.60 baht Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers attributed the scramble for dollars to investor fears of a further baht fall. Since the Bank of Thailand abandoned the fixed-exchange rate regime, the baht has lost 32% of its value against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  'Many people decided to dump the baht as soon as the dollar broke above 35 baht,' a dealer at Hongkong & Shanghai Banking Corp. Ltd said. 'They were afraid that the dollar will rise to as high as 40 baht.' \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand, moving to prop up the baht, offered to sell dollars to commercial banks between 36.00 and 36.50 baht in the afternoon, dealers said. However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's effort proved futile as investors continued to dump the baht in favor of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  just rolled the ball into investors' court,' said a dealer at a Japanese bank in Bangkok. 'People were happy to buy dollars from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  because they got it cheaper than the market's rate.' \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 03-09-97 \par \par \uc2  1110GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt9306hk8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
