\par\par \b \uc2  Thai  \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervenes \highlight\uc2  to halt baht slide. \b0\par\par\uc2 266 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 September 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Sept 3 (Reuter) - The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through primary local banks to halt a rapid slide in the baht on Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The baht, which had briefly hit 37.00 per dollar around midday, was being quoted at 35.50/36.00 per dollar at 0644 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "I see no other reason for the baht to come back to this level but \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  through the primary local banks," said a dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier said the baht's rapid slide on Wednesday took the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a level inconsistent with Thailand's economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  The baht slipped to 36.50/37.50 per dollar from 35.15/35.25 late on Tuesday as corporates continued buying dollars in anticipation of the baht's further weakness and refusal of Thai exporters to liquidate dollar holdings, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said thin volumes increased market volatility. Some players said they believed the baht's sell-off looked over-extended at 37.00. \par \par \uc2  "The highest bid was around 37.20 but I think that's a bit overdone," said a spot dealer at a large foreign bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  "This morning the corporates were taking any quote they could get thinking it was going to go lower but exporters were holding back. Volumes were pretty thin so it's not taking much to move market 50 satang or so," he said. \par \par \uc2  --Bangkok newsroom (662) 642-0642 \par \par \uc2  --e-mail: bangkok.newsroom@reuters.com REUTER jam 