\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand/Shares End -2: Little Joy From  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 311 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 1997\par 11:54\par \uc2  Dow Jones Asian Equities Report \par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the worries over capital increases were aggravated after Siam City Bank PCL said Wednesday it was doubling its registered capital to 12 billion baht to help finance a merger between its affiliated finance companies. Investors worried that there will be more to come in the banking sector, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Bank of Thailand's latest economic indicators offered little relief. Analysts said the figures mostly weighed in as expected. \par \par \uc2  Under its new commitment to release foreign reserves figures every two weeks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said that as of Aug. 15, its foreign reserves were at $27.9 billion baht. This is a three-year low, and investors took it as a sign that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will see more declines in its foreign reserves resulting from its failed attempt to defend the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from speculative attack. The baht was freed from its fixed peg against the dollar on July 2, and has since lost over 20% of its value. \par \par \uc2  Last week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had outstanding obligations of $23.4 billion baht in the swap markets. This market, where investors agree to buy and sell baht at set rates at given times in the future, was the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's preferred way of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. As these forward contracts become due, analysts fear Thailand's foreign reserves could fall as low as $10 billion. The country now has over $17 billion in standby credit from the International Monetary Fund and sovereign states to help top up its foreign reserves. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       Thursday     Previous    Change\par SET Index             511.76       523.74      -11.98\par SET 50 Index          36.84        37.95       -1.11\par Dow Jones Thailand    58.57        60.49       -1.92\par Index $ (Late)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) DOW JONES ASIAN EQUITIES REPORT  28-08-97\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0954GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  5048 55107 \par \par \uc2 Dokument aer0000020011004dt8s0156k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
