\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht resumes fall, drags down other  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 667 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 August 1997\par 06:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 22 (Reuter) - Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed renewed signs of weakness on Friday as falls of the Thai baht and Indonesian rupiah infected the others. \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht hit a record low of 33.30 in domestic markets on heavy commercial demand for dollars and nagging concerns about the country's economic and political outlook. \par \par \uc2  "Some corporates might buy dollars to pay back foreign loans coming due. The volume (of dollar purchases) is quite substantial," a Bangkok dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The baht was at 33.13/32 to the dollar at 0410 GMT against 32.65/75 late on Thursday. The offshore rate followed suit, sliding to 32.80/33.00 against 32.30/50. \par \par \uc2  "With 33 being broken, the sky's the limit. It's in uncharted territory," the head of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a European bank in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  He said the baht looked set to hit 35 to the dollar and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOT) was unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the slide. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is very tied up with the IMF (International Monetary Fund) package. And as long as they're able to maintain the two-tier regime, the market will not dare to push the baht in a big way because there's not much liquidity," he said. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, BOT Governor Chaiyawat Wibulswasdi said Thailand would receive $1.6 billion in loans immediately as the first installment of the IMF's $3.9 billion loan package.He also pledged to meet the IMF's economic goals to receive further aid. \par \par \uc2  In Indonesia, the rupiah weakened anew as players covered short dollar positions ahead of the weekend and local companies sought to hedge their positions. \par \par \uc2  "The funds are buying the dollar again after liquidating their positions above the 2,900 level," the Singapore dealer said. Sentiment was also depressed by Standard and Poor's announcement on Thursday that it had revised the ratings outlook on Indonesian banks to negative from stable, he added. \par \par \uc2  Reports of a run on deposits at one of Indonesia's banks were also affecting the market, he said. \par \par \uc2  Spot rupiah was at 2,735/45 at 0410 GMT against 2,675/75 late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  A Japanese bank dealer in Jakarta said the rupiah showed scope to strengthen through the 2,700 level again as the outlook for liquidity remained tight. \par \par \uc2  "Liquidity is still the main concern. Operators are also preparing for Monday because the previous \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  forward \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will mature," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Malaysian ringgit surrendered early gains and fell sharply on spillover from the rupiah and baht, though thin volumes and wide spreads continued to exaggerate activity. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was at 2.7700/20 to the dollar after reaching a high of 2.7430 earlier, against 2.7650/700 late on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar slid back through the 1.50 to the U.S. dollar level and dealers said a breach of 1.5040 could trigger fresh buying of the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  "But the pace will be slower as the market is looking more favourably at the Singapore dollar than the other regionals," a dealer said, citing strong Singapore export figures announced on Wednesday and an upward revision of its 1997 growth forecast. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso recovered from a weak start as exporters and other companies converted foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposits to pesos following recent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves to tighten liquidity. \par \par \uc2  The peso was at 29.79/85 to the dollar against Thursday's close of 29.885. \par \par \uc2  In Taiwan, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's prolonged defence of the T$28.727 level in the face of offshore speculative pressure finally dampened demand for U.S. dollars. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar showed a firm bias and was quoted at T$28.724/726 against Thursday's T$28.724 close. \par \par \uc2  Taipei dealers said inflows of foreign equity funds to the recovering stock market also helped the recovery. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8m00rig\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
