\par\par \b \uc2  Profit taking pushes S.E Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  higher. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 671 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 August 1997\par 06:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 1 (Reuter) - Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rocked by weeks of turmoil, firmed on Friday morning as players cashed in some of their gains on the dollar ahead of the weekend. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said players were reluctant to establish new positions ahead of the release of Thailand's economic rescue plan, due by August 5, which is expected to include assistance from the International Monetary Fund (IMF). \par \par \uc2  "Everybody wants to see what the IMF will do in Thailand on the fifth because that will indirectly affect all the other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a Singapore-based trader said. \par \par \uc2  Vague rumours of an impending military coup in Thailand hit New York markets overnight, causing sales of dollar/baht and a rise in swap premiums. But the rumours had been around for weeks and little credence was attached to them, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  One said there was talk the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell the dollar around 32.10 baht in Singapore markets on Friday. No confirmation was available. \par \par \uc2  The baht slipped back a notch from morning highs after Standard & Poor's Corp placed Thailand's "A" long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rating on creditwatch. \par \par \uc2  That was further bad news for the Thai economy, implying greater than expected loan losses in the crisis-torn financial sector. \par \par \uc2  The baht was quoted at 31.85/31.95 to the dollar onshore at 0435 GMT against 31.700/9500 late on Thursday. The offshore rate was at 31.80/32.00. \par \par \uc2  In Malaysia, the ringgit showed little immediate reaction to news Bank Negara Malaysia had asked banks to hold their base lending rates steady. \par \par \uc2  Banking sources in Kuala Lumpur said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had asked them to hold their base lending rates at 9.67 percent despite a recent spike up in interbank rates. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was at 2.6245/95 to the dollar after firming through the 2.63 level earlier on profit-taking in the dollar by funds. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar looked firm against the ringgit, but talk of large orders to sell the dollar at the 2.6400 level was likely to limit its rise. \par \par \uc2  The market was awaiting Malaysia's trade data for June, expected next week, amid talk of a 1.5 billion ringgit deficit after May's surplus of 157 million ringgit. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar rose through the key 1.47 level to the U.S. dollar but dealers said its rise was likely to be capped around 1.4650. \par \par \uc2  "This is probably just profit-taking. I'm still looking at a higher dollar/Sing," a dealer said, adding that the market continued to expect the Sing to drop to around 1.50. \par \par \uc2  Trade in the Indonesian rupiah was slow, dominated by covering of short dollar positions for the weekend. Spot rupiah was at 2,605/15 against an opening of 2,613/23. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso was firmer as banks scrambled to meet a deadline to cut long dollar positions after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  slashed the long dollar limit of banks to five percent of capital from 10 percent, or 10 million, whichever is lower. \par \par \uc2  Newspapers quoted \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Gabriel Singson as saying he expected banks to unload $200 million due to the new ruling. The peso was at 28.960/29.060 against its previous close at 29. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar slipped back from an early high of T$28.590, inspired by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move to raise two key interest rates after the market's close on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the rediscount rate to 5.25 percent from 5.00 percent and accomodations against secured loans to 5.625 percent from 5.375 percent, effective from Friday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sheu Yuan-dong said the rate hikes were aimed at maintaining stability in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was at T$28.653/660 against Thursday's close at T$28.70, its weakest finish since 1988. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt8101qkn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
