\par\par \b \uc2  FOCUS - Thai baht dives to record low,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Rajan Moses \par \uc2 603 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 1997\par 13:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, July 23 (Reuter) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's beleaguered baht plunged to a record low in the local market on Wednesday, forcing \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to arrest the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's worst slide since it went into a managed float on July 2. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the baht's dive in the thinly traded onshore market was mainly due to a scramble for dollars by local importers seeking the U.S. unit to pay bills and by corporates needing the greenback to repay foreign loans. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers reported baht/dollar deals done at a level as low as 32.60 to the dollar before the Bank of Thailand's defence of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  through dollar sales. \par \par \uc2  "We noticed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the baht's fall at around the 32.50/32.60 (bid/ask) to the dollar level," a senior dealer with a local bank told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  Others said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not have to sell many dollars to curb the baht's fall. \par \par \uc2  This was because pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was mainly from local players trading in relatively small amounts and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's movement was exaggerated in a thin market. \par \par \uc2  After the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by around 0925 GMT, the baht steadied and was quoted at around 32.21/32.41 against the dollar in the domestic market and stronger at 31.45/31.55 in the offshore market. \par \par \uc2  Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials were not available for comment on the reported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stock market plummeted more than four percent, in part due to worries about the baht, brokers said. It closed down 28.50 points to 631.28. \par \par \uc2  The baht's tumble comes as Thailand goes through its worst economic slump in more than a decade and its financial sector faces numerous troubles. \par \par \uc2  The baht was released into a managed float by Thailand after being pegged for 13 years to a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dominated by the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Since the flotation, the baht has undergone a de facto devaluation of about 20 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers and a senior Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official also attributed poor baht sentiment to weak first-half earnings results reported by local banks and finance firms this week. \par \par \uc2  "I think this is mainly a result of the bank's results we saw yesterday and that knocked the fragile confidence that had crept back in," said one Singapore based analyst. \par \par \uc2  "If you look at the results of the banks there are some horror stories in terms of earnings per share." \par \par \uc2  With the corporate market still squeezed there was still a cash-flow problem. That, on top of the bad balance sheet issue made worse by the devaluation of offshore liabilities, had led to a scramble for dollars in short supply, he said. \par \par \uc2  Thanasak Chantarovat, deputy director of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's banking department, said the baht could also have been hurt by negative expectations about data on the level of non-performing loans of financial institutions due to be released soon. \par \par \uc2  The data is due to be announced through the stock exchange on Thursday, a local banker said. \par \par \uc2  Financial markets have been waiting nervously to gauge the level of non-performing loans by banks and finance firms, which are overexposed with billions of dollars in sour loans to the depressed and cash-strapped property sector. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers said they saw an appropriate level for the baht at between 30.50-31.50 to the dollar in the near term, given current concerns over the Thai economy and problems in the financial sector. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7n021pf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
