\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht quoted at new record low against dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 369 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, July 23 (Reuter) - The Thai baht was quoted on Wednesday at a new record low of 32.15/32.50 against the dollar as players sought refuge in the greenback, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Some foreign and local banks onshore were quoting the baht at new lows to test the resolve of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  and see if it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to stabilise the sliding \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , they added. "There is so far no sign of any \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a dealer with a local bank told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  In the offshore market, the baht was quoted higher at 31.20/31.40 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on July 2, after it freed the baht from its peg to a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  dominated by the dollar and allowed it into a managed float, that it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the baht fell to an "appropriate level". \par \par \uc2  When the baht hit around 30 to the dollar last week, a top \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said it had fallen low enough. \par \par \uc2  Earlier on Wednesday, the baht fell to its previous record low of 31.60 on talk that commercial demand for dollars had dampened baht sentiment in a thin market. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials declined to comment on any plans to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop the baht up. \par \par \uc2  But one official said the baht's drop was exaggerated because of the thinness of trade in the market. \par \par \uc2  Thanasak Chantarovat, deputy director of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's banking department, told reporters that the baht slide on Wednesday was aggravated by poor first-half earnings of commercial banks and finance companies. \par \par \uc2  He said the weak bank earnings stemmed from their required higher reserves for doubtful loans but he added that the increased provisions would strengthen banks in the long run. \par \par \uc2  The official said sentiment on the baht could also be hurt by expectations that data on the level of non-performing loans of financial institutions would be released soon to the stock market. \par \par \uc2  "They could have negative psychological effect if the figures are high but I don't think they would be that bad," he said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7n021h4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
