\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand Baht Ends In All-Time Low On Strong Dlr Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 356 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 1997\par 13:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht plunged to its all-time low against the dollar Wednesday, hurt by brisk dollar buying by Thai corporations nervous about the continued depreciation of the baht, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, strengthened in the swap market, where investors make agreements to buy and sell baht at specified times in the future. Swap premiums dropped. \par \par \uc2  At the close of Asian trading Wednesday, the dollar was at 32.30 baht in the domestic market - believed to be a historic closing high for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, this was still below the afternoon high of 32.50 baht, which was the all-time high. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at 31.00 baht Tuesday. In the offshore market, the dollar closed at 31.55 baht, up from 30.60 baht Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers attributed the baht's historical decline to a scramble for dollars among Thai corporations, which have an estimated $45 billion in short-term loans. \par \par \uc2  'Demand for dollars was purely commercial,' said a dealer at a U.S. bank in Bangkok. 'Thai companies still owe a lot of money to foreign lenders, and importers still need dollars to pay for their imports.' \par \par \uc2  At the closing level, the dollar was well above the 30-baht range at which the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the baht. Even so, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  did little to prop up the baht Wednesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  'There was some \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  through Thai banks, but I don't think it was to reverse the trend,' said a dealer at a Hong Kong bank in Bangkok. 'I think the (\b \highlight22\uc2 central) bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  just wanted to keep the baht from falling too sharply against the dollar.' \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand set its reference rate for the dollar at 30.842 baht, up from 30.370 baht Tuesday. The reference rate is a weighted average of rates charged by Thai commercial banks the previous day. It serves as a benchmark for domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1121GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7n05hqa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
