\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand Baht Falls Early On Strong Corporate Dlr-Buying \b0\par\par\uc2 362 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Juli 1997\par 04:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht fell against the dollar in both domestic and offshore dealings early Wednesday as Thai corporations continued to snap up dollars to hedge and repay their foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  loans, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, is mixed in the swap market, where investors make agreements to buy and sell baht at specified times in the future. One- and two-month and one-year swap premiums are lower but the three- and six-month rates are higher. \par \par \uc2  At 0230 GMT (10:30 p.m. EDT), the dollar is at 31.30 baht in the domestic spot market, up from 31.00 baht at the close of trading Tuesday. In the offshore market, however, the dollar is at 30.85 baht, up from 30.60 baht Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the baht continued to weaken amid persistent dollar-buying by Thai corporations, which have an estimated $45 billion in short-term loans. The Bank of Thailand's decision to let the baht float July 2, they said, adds debt obligations to the private sector. \par \par \uc2  'Trading in the market has been purely demand-driven these days,' said a dealer at a U.S. bank in Bangkok. 'The most active players in the market have been Thai companies seeking to build up dollar position to pay their debts.' \par \par \uc2  At the current spot rate, the dollar is well above 30 baht, the level at which the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the baht. However, dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't been selling dollars to prop up the baht lately. 'The Bank of Thailand has been careful with their reserves,' said one dealer. Others said the bank may be comfortable to see the baht ranging between 30 and 31 baht. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand set its reference rate for the dollar at 30.842 baht, up from 30.370 baht Tuesday. The reference rate is a weighted average of rates charged by Thai commercial banks the previous day. It serves as a benchmark for domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 23-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0247GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7n05eea\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
