\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand not seeking IMF loans, officials say. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Vithoon Amorn \par \uc2 418 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 1997\par 12:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, July 16 (Reuter) - Bank of Thailand and finance ministry officials said on Wednesday that Thailand has not considered seeking loans from the International Monetary Fund (IMF) to help ease its liquidity and economic problems. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokeswoman Duangmanee Wongprateep said Thailand had not asked for financial assistance from an IMF team now visiting the country. The team is in Thailand to help assess government measures for bailing out cash-strapped or troubled financial institutions. \par \par \uc2  "In theory, (an IMF loan) is an option open to us but we have not moved to consider seeking one from them," she told Reuters. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials said a separate IMF team has visited Thailand to provide technical advice on how to implement the baht's managed float policy. The baht was floated on July 2. \par \par \uc2  Thailand let its baht depreciate sharply early this month after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  faced speculative pressure for several weeks. \par \par \uc2  Finance ministry sources said an IMF loan was still not required despite Thailand's current economic downturn, the worst in over a decade. \par \par \uc2  "No move has been made (on borrowing from the IMF). Such a need would arise if our foreign reserves were greatly depleted but it is premature to say our reserves have plunged because of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (to defend the baht)," a finance ministry official said. \par \par \uc2  He said some of the forward baht/dollar positions taken by the Bank of Thailand in May in defence of the baht had still not matured, making it difficult to determine how much \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would use in its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Borrowing from the IMF would subject \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to certain austerity conditions and we should consider them first," he said. \par \par \uc2  However, analysts said that while Thailand may not need IMF financial assistance it could benefit from loans by the agency because these would be viewed by the financial market as a stamp of approval of the country's economic adjustment policies. \par \par \uc2  The Thai stock market rallied sharply on Wednesday as regional funds moved into the bourse on hopes that the IMF may be preparing to step in and help the economy. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Thanong Bidaya and Bank of Thailand Governor Rerngchai Marakanond go to Tokyo on Wednesday night for talks with their Japanese counterparts on the country's economic situation. \par \par \uc2  Japan appears to have linked financial aid for Thailand's ailing economy to IMF involvement in its economic management. \par \par \uc2  -- Bangkok newsroom (662)-6520642 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7g02lm0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
