\par\par \b \uc2  Thai c.bank confirms  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  to help baht. \b0\par\par\uc2 396 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, July 14 (Reuter) - Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rerngchai Marakanond on Monday confirmed market talk and said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars to help stem the baht's fall against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, but in a very small way. This caused the baht to stabilise in the afternoon," Rerngchai told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Rerngchai also said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  planned to keep the two-tier \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and its current strict capital controls to prevent any further attack on the baht. \par \par \uc2  Rerngchai was speaking after meeting Prime Minister Chavalit Yongchaiyudh, former finance minister Amnuay Viravan and senior officials from the government's think-tank, the National Economic and Social Development Board (NESDB). \par \par \uc2  The governor said the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, which has been jolted by the crisis in other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was expected to return to normal in the next one to two days. \par \par \uc2  "The baht is at very low level and will stay at around 30 baht for some time. But the market should calm down in the next one to two days," Rerngchai said. \par \par \uc2  The baht fell sharply to new record low of 30.80 to the dollar on Monday morning on a spillover effect of speculative attacks on other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The baht recovered ground in the afternoon, to trade at around 29.85/30.00 in mid-afternoon in the onshore market compared with 30.30/30.75 in early dealings. \par \par \uc2  The baht was also buoyed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor Chaiyawat Wilbulsawasdi's statement earlier that the baht had fallen to a level that was low enough and the bank would take action to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stop wild fluctuations. \par \par \uc2  NESDB's secretary general Wirat Wattanasirtham said preliminary figures showed Thailand's gross domestic product would grow at a mere 4.6 percent this year if the baht were to fall by 10 percent. \par \par \uc2  He said the current account deficit would be at about 5.0-5.5 percent of GDP if the baht dropped 10 percent. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand said on Monday the baht had fallen about 15 percent since it switched to a managed float on July 2 from the previous system of pegging it to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7e02q8w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
