\par\par \b \uc2  Southeast Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  under siege. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sonali Desai \par \uc2 627 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1997\par 06:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, July 14 (Reuter) - Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were hit by waves of selling on Monday as uncertainty following the Philippine peso's effective devaluation last week spread like wildfire through the region. \par \par \uc2  In Malaysia, the ringgit fell to a 16-month low of 2.5500 to the dollar in early trade amid Bank Negara Malaysia's failure to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The ringgit was quoted at 2.5375/95 to the dollar at 0400 GMT against 2.5042/52 at its Kuala Lumpur close on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "It's crazy," a European bank dealer in Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  "Because of the story of the Philippine peso, which they devalued last week, the market is expecting the ringgit and rupiah to follow suit," she added. \par \par \uc2  Another European bank dealer in Singapore said Bank Negara was heard to have sold dollars around the 2.5500 ringgit level. "But I think Negara was in just to slow down the fall rather than stop the flow," he said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market was still long of dollars, leaving room for the ringgit to head lower. \par \par \uc2  They said Bank Negara may be allowing market forces to dictate the spot's value rather than defending the ringgit aggressively in the face of heavy selling interest. \par \par \uc2  Dealers estimate the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent over $1 billion to support the ringgit last week. \par \par \uc2  In Indonesia, the rupiah rebounded from its early lows as offshore players began unloading dollars. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said offshore players seemed to be trying to cash out from the market after they drove the rupiah to a low of 2,469.0 on Monday morning. \par \par \uc2  "I think some feel that the rupiah is low enough for a buy back, reversing the market trend," a local bank dealer in Jakarta said. \par \par \uc2  But another local bank dealer said the rupiah buying was initiated by some state banks and followed through by offshore players, driving the rupiah to a high of 2,445 before operators bought some dollars back. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was quoted at 2,453.0/58.0 at 0400 GMT against an opening 2,451.0/55.0. \par \par \uc2  "Bank Indonesia (BI)'s band widening last week is not helping to strengthen the rupiah. With BI having the lowest reserves, the rupiah will be the next \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to attack," a Singapore-based dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  widened its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band to 12 percent from eight percent last Friday, in what was seen as a move to pre-empt possible turbulence in the rupiah after speculative attacks on the peso and baht. \par \par \uc2  In the Philippines, the peso fell to a low of 29.75 to the dollar in thin trade as banks remained wary after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's move on Friday to allow the peso-dollar rate to trade within a wider band. \par \par \uc2  Volume was a light nine million dollars after two-and-a-half hours of trading on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOT) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the baht's fall in domestic markets, selling dollars at the 30.75-30.80 baht level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  through a small local bank by selling the dollar at around 30.75-30.80," a European bank dealer in Bangkok said. \par \par \uc2  A BOT spokeswoman declined to say whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  Commercial dollar demand and lingering jitters from the peso slide pushed the baht to new lows. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 30.500/30.800 to the dollar in the domestic market at 0400 GMT, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , against 30.00/30.60 late on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "The amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was insignificant. But it capped the baht at around 30.80," the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7e02q3g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
