\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht seen fragile despite  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Anuchit Nguyen \par \uc2 504 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1997\par 13:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, July 14 (Reuter) - The Thai baht is likely to hit new lows in coming months despite the Bank of Thailand's insistence that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sunk far enough, analysts said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's vow on Monday to support the baht would not be enough to withstand an erosion of foreign investor confidence in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the de facto devaluation of the Philippine peso and the Thai baht in recent weeks, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "The baht will remain fragile in the short term. It's largely due to uncertainty across the region as a lot of people are taking (funds) out of the region," Jimmy Koh at Singapore-based research house I.D.E.A. told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "By the end of this year, I expect the baht to be around 31-32 to the dollar," Koh said. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's worst economic downturn in over a decade and near crisis in the finance sector would add pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said. \par \par \uc2  "It will take time for the economy to pick up and the financial crisis to be resolved. In the short term, the pressure on the baht will still persist," said Ali Seng at MMS International. \par \par \uc2  Seng said the baht was expected to fall to about 31-33 baht per dollar by the end of this year, echoing expectations of a number of other analysts. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said there were also worries about the quality of assets owned by financial institutions after the baht's de facto devaluation and their overexposure to cash-strapped property firms. \par \par \uc2  Deputy Bank of Thailand Governor Chaiyawat Wibulsawasdi said on Monday he believed the baht's current level of 30 to the dollar was low enough. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would take action to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stop more wild fluctuations, he added. \par \par \uc2  "It is our direct responsibility to take measures to do anything that will help stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate and ease volatility in the market," he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rerngchai Marakanond on Monday confirmed the bank had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the baht's slide against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  "We \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, but in a very small way. This caused the baht to stabilise in the afternoon," Rerngchai told reporters. \par \par \uc2  This is the first time since the adoption of the managed float \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  system for the baht on July 2 that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to defend the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 , via a small local bank, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the domestic market and sold dollars at the record low level of 30.75-30.80 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  The baht was quoted at a record low of around 30.30/30.80 per dollar early on Monday in the domestic market compared with 30.00/30.60 late on Friday. \par \par \uc2  After the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and statement, the baht recovered significantly to trade at around 29.70/30.20 in late afternoon. \par \par \uc2