\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht recovers after  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , statement. \b0\par\par\uc2 125 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1997\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, July 14 (Reuter) - The Thai baht rose sharply in late trade on Monday after dropping to a record low in morning trade after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and said the baht had already fallen to a very low level, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The baht significantly improved in the afternoon. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and its statement helped boost confidence (in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 )," said one foreign bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The baht was quoted at 29.00/30.00 near the close in the domestic market compared with 30.30/30.75 early. The baht fell to 30.80 early, prompting the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars around 30.75/30.80, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7e02pze\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
