\par\par \b \uc2  Thai baht plunges, spurs  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , stocks fall. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Deborah Charles \par \uc2 550 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1997\par 13:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1997 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, July 14 (Reuter) - Jittery regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  drove Thailand's newly floated baht to a record low against the dollar on Monday, spurring \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and causing shivers in the local bourse. \par \par \uc2  For the first time since announcing a surprise, de facto devaluation on July 2, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to stem the baht's steep fall against the dollar. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Rerngchai Marakanond confirmed market talk of an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and said the bank had sold dollars to help stabilise the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, but in a very small way," Rerngchai told reporters. "This caused the tumbling baht to stabilise in the afternoon." \par \par \uc2  The baht fell sharply to a record low of 30.80 to the dollar in morning trade on a spillover effect of speculative attacks on other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. It recovered ground late to trade around 29.25/29.75 bid/ask offshore and 29.90/30.00 in domestic markets. \par \par \uc2  Rergnchai said he thought the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market had been jolted by regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and said it should stabilise in the next day or two. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deputy governor, Chaiyawat Wibulsawasdi, said the Bank of Thailand decided the baht had fallen low enough when it dived over 30 baht to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  When it announced a change to a managed float from its 13-year-old regime of pegging the baht to a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  as required to keep the baht at an appropriate level. \par \par \uc2  Chaiyawat said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had dropped 15 percent, in terms of the average daily interbank rate, since the float was implemented on July 2. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's determination to stick to its policy of "managing" the float failed to convince equities punters. \par \par \uc2  The bourse, which lost more than four percent of its value last week, dropped 2.65 percent on Monday in thin dealings as investors unloaded large capitalised stocks on fears the baht would lose more ground, brokers and analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The Stock Exchange of Thailand's key index ended down 16.64 at 611.91 points in thin turnover of 3.4 billion baht. \par \par \uc2  "Investors believe that the baht isn't yet stable and will slip further from today," said one broker. "They think it's risky to hold baht at present." \par \par \uc2  Several major Thai companies face huge exchange losses this year, analysts said. At 30 baht per dollar Siam Cement Plc, the country's largest conglomerate, faces exchange losses of 9.9 billion baht on its unhedged foreign loans. \par \par \uc2  "Every bit the baht goes down makes a lot of these companies lose more and more," said one analyst. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said they needed to see more concrete signs that the Thai economy -- growing at its slowest pace in a decade -- was on the road to recovery before the stock market would pick up. \par \par \uc2  A finance ministry official said on Monday Thailand would not rule out seeking financial assistance from the International Monetary Fund to help solve its economic problems. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said any such borrowing would be accompanied by painful conditions but it was necessary for Thailand to have a credit life-line. \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1997 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dt7e02pzc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
