\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand Baht Climbs Late As Central Bk Pledges Its Support \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1997\par 13:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--The Thai baht strengthened against the dollar in the domestic market Monday after the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stop the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falling below 30 baht to the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  But the baht weakened offshore, with investors overseas still concerned about further attacks on the baht after the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave up its defense of the ringgit, which had kept the Malaysian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 2.5250 ringgit to the dollar for weeks. \par \par \uc2  The baht also weakened in the swap market, where investors agree to buy and sell baht at specified times in the future. Swap premiums rose. \par \par \uc2  At the close of domestic trading Monday, the dollar was at 29.90 baht, down from 30.75 baht Friday. In the offshore market, the dollar was higher at 29.80 baht, compared with 29.25 baht Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Thailand set its reference rate at 29.945 baht, up from 29.155 baht Friday. The reference rate is a weighted average of rates charged by Thai commercial banks the previous day. It serves as a benchmark for domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading. \par \par \uc2  At a press conference called Monday, the Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the markets to stop the Thai baht falling below 30 baht to the dollar. If it falls past that mark, analysts have said it could inflict severe damage on Thai companies with extensive foreign loans. Siam Cement PCL, the country's largest industrial conglomerate, last week said it would lose up to 9.9 billion baht if the baht settles at 30 baht against the greenback. \par \par \uc2  'I believe the Bank of Thailand was selling dollars to back up their announcement today,' one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  (END) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-07-97 \par \par \uc2  1100GMT \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7e054ku\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
