\par\par \b \uc2  Thailand:UBS Sees Foreign Reserves Dn To $15B By End Of '97 \b0\par\par\uc2 317 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1997\par 10:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK (AP-Dow Jones)--Thailand's foreign reserves could dwindle by more than 50% to $15 billion by the end of the year as a result of continued \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop the Thai baht, the Union Bank of Switzerland has predicted. \par \par \uc2  The bank said in a report obtained by Dow Jones Monday that the U.S. dollar could rise as high as 33 baht by the end of the year, up from about 30 baht now. The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Monday it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars to prevent the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rising above 30 baht. \par \par \uc2  'The demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be large over the next 12 to 24 months...,' UBS said. Without a resumption of strong capital inflows, 'the baht will come under renewed strong pressure - something the (Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) can only temporarily offset through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .' \par \par \uc2  By law, \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs at least $8 billion in reserves to back up its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Its reserves stood at $33.3 billion at the end of May, a two-year low. UBS has estimated Thailand will need to borrow between $20 billion and $40 billion from international lenders such as the International Monetary Fund to shore up reserves and stabilize cash-strapped financial institutions. \par \par \uc2  UBS said Thailand has outstanding short-term debt of $42 billion to $45 billion, most of it owed by the private sector. 'As the credit standing of Thai firms deteriorates, there will be added pressure to resort to onshore borrowing as offshore credit sources dry up,' UBS said. It said Thailand also has $8 billion to $12 billion in long-term debt that matures in the next year. In the same period, the bank said, the country will also need $8 billion to finance its current account deficit. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 14-07-97 \par \par \uc2  0828GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011006dt7e05453\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Thailand near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\